<interrogationes unitas="arbor2_token">

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I find the source line and column a macro-expanded token came from?
    <responsum symbolum="arbor2_token_radix Arbor2OrigoMeta" via="lib/arbor2_glr.c">Walk
      the chain with arbor2_token_radix, which follows origo_token
      until it is NIHIL, and read radix-&gt;origo_meta-&gt;linea,
      columna and via_file. For a token expanded from a macro the
      root is the source token of the outermost invocation, so the
      position is the call site, not the macro body; arbor2_glr does
      exactly this to give every node its location. Tokens of a macro
      ARGUMENT are not rewrapped: arbor2_expandere copies the caller's
      own tokens into the expansion, so they resolve to their own
      place inside the argument list. A token that is already a source
      token (or an API token) is its own root.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I get both input tokens of a ## paste?
    <responsum symbolum="arbor2_token_pasta arbor2_token_ex_pasta Arbor2OrigoPasta">arbor2_token_pasta
      returns the token's origo_meta as an Arbor2OrigoPasta (sinister
      and dexter) when its genus is ARBOR2_ORIGO_PASTA, NIHIL
      otherwise. The ordinary chain (origo_token, and so
      arbor2_token_radix) follows only the LEFT token: the right one
      is reachable only through dexter.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can origo_meta or nomen_macro be NIHIL on a token?
    <responsum symbolum="arbor2_token_ex_lexema arbor2_token_ex_expansione arbor2_token_ex_api">origo_meta,
      never, for tokens made by the arbor2_token_ex_* constructors: it
      is always allocated with piscina_allocare (fatal on
      failure: the process exits), so no NIHIL checks are needed.
      nomen_macro is NIHIL for source tokens; via_file may be NIHIL
      (arbor2_token_ex_api allows it, and expansions copy whatever the
      macro definition stored). The constructors copy neither the
      lexema nor the chordae: the token points at the caller's, so
      they must live as long as the token.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what is the difference between arbor2_token_est_fons, layer_index and arbor2_token_profunditas?
    <responsum symbolum="arbor2_token_est_fons arbor2_token_profunditas arbor2_origo_genus_nomen Arbor2OrigoGenus">arbor2_token_est_fons
      tests the genus (ARBOR2_ORIGO_FONS), not the layer, despite the
      header's "(layer 0)" comment; argument tokens copied into an
      expansion are still FONS, so it is VERUM for them.
      layer_index is a number the caller passes in (source tokens get
      0). arbor2_token_profunditas counts the origo_token links back
      to the root (0 for a source or API token). For log output,
      arbor2_origo_genus_nomen turns a genus into FONS, EXPANSIO,
      PASTA, CHORDA or API (IGNOTUM when out of range).</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>where do linea and columna of an expanded or stringified token come from?
    <responsum symbolum="arbor2_token_ex_expansione arbor2_token_ex_chorda arbor2_token_ex_lexema">From
      origo_token-&gt;lexema (the invoking token's own lexeme position,
      1-based), or 0 when origo_token is NIHIL; a ## result takes the
      left token's. For a macro called from source that is the call
      site, but when the invoking token itself came from an outer
      macro's body, its lexeme position is where the name sits in the
      outer #define. Use arbor2_token_radix for the call site.
      arbor2_token_ex_lexema
      takes linea and columna explicitly, and callers pass
      lexema-&gt;linea and lexema-&gt;columna. API tokens always get
      0.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I tell from a token that it came from a macro added through the API?
    <responsum symbolum="arbor2_token_ex_api arbor2_expansion_addere_macro arbor2_expansion_addere_macro_functio Arbor2MacroDef">Not
      from the token: nothing calls arbor2_token_ex_api, so no token
      ever has genus ARBOR2_ORIGO_API. Macros added with
      arbor2_expansion_addere_macro or _functio expand through
      arbor2_token_ex_expansione like any other, giving EXPANSIO
      tokens whose via_file is NIHIL when no file was passed. The
      flag lives on the definition instead: Arbor2MacroDef ex_api is
      VERUM for API macros.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
